{"name":"Crusoe","hex":"#165b31","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Crusoe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from French, famously held by:","A male given name transferred from the surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Crusoe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crusoe (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Crusoe is a 1988 British drama film directed by Caleb Deschanel. It is a variation on the story told in the 1719 novel Robinson Crusoe by Daniel Defoe. The film stars Aidan Quinn as Crusoe."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Crusoe_%281988_movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crusoe_(film)"},{"title":"Crusoe (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Crusoe is an adventure-drama television series, based loosely on the 1719 novel Robinson Crusoe by Daniel Defoe. The series' 13 episodes aired on NBC from October 17, 2008, to January 31, 2009, during the first half of the 2008–09 television season. It follows the adventures of Robinson Crusoe: a man who has been shipwrecked on an island for six years and is desperate to return home to his wife and children. His lone companion is Friday, a native whom Crusoe rescued and taught English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/27/Crusoe-title.jpg/330px-Crusoe-title.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crusoe_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/Crusoe_%281988_movie_poster%29.jpg/250px-Crusoe_%281988_movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Crusoe_%281988_movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/Crusoe_%2